The updated Notification Service plan looks solid and aligns well with a scalable event-driven microservice architecture. The use of a single RabbitMQ queue with topic routing simplifies event consumption while maintaining flexibility for multiple event types. Adding retry handling with DLQ improves reliability, and integrating a dedicated SignalR Hub for realtime delivery is appropriate for a notification system. The decision to map entities to DTOs before pushing via SignalR also ensures the API responses remain consistent with the frontend contract. Using Redis for unread notification count is a good optimization to reduce database load.

One important note: **actor resolution should only call the UserProfile service** to retrieve user information (name, avatar, role). There is no need to call multiple services for this. The notification service should remain lightweight and avoid unnecessary cross-service dependencies. Adding a small in-memory cache for the resolved actor data (for a few minutes) would further reduce repeated service calls and improve performance.
